			"notes": "* Added `/nrss`, which lets you **start a route to a station based on its name** instead of the code. Only supports routes from current location to keep command parsing simple.\n* Added **suggestions when typing** the command to start a route.\n* Added the ability to set a custom network file. Can be set using the config screen or `/nrs config network_file URL`. This lets you e.g. set a file on your computer as the source of the NguhRoutes data instead of the wiki one. Primarily intended for testing without messing with the wiki file.\n* You can now actually start a route that involves codes with ???, spaces or other weird characters in them. Use quotes for codes with spaces in them. This is intended for temporary codes, not an encouragement to make codes with funky characters in them."
		},
